<title>USA: US high-yield mutual fund cash flows up latest wk.</title>
<headline>US high-yield mutual fund cash flows up latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investors extended the longstanding trend of net inflows to U.S. high-yield mutual funds in the latest week, although the rate remained below the heady pace seen earlier this year, sources said.</p>
<p>Cash inflows to high-yield funds that report on a weekly basis totaled $194 million in the week ended Wednesday, according to AMG Data Services, the sources said. The figure compares with inflows of $152 million for the previous week and $527 two weeks prior.</p>
<p>AMG Data was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
